      "message": "Does this vary? I believe the reason `stretch` was used is because it is defined to vary, but I\u0027m not sure that this value varies with `wdth`? We should make sure we have a test for that actually... the TypefaceStyle ensures that we get the expected values from a non-variable font, but I don\u0027t see a test currently that ensures a variable font non-default `wdth` produces the expected width values. Note that we can use the existing `Variable.ttf` test font for this since it has both `wght` and `wdth`.\n\nNote on the FreeType side this is done in SkFontScanner_FreeType::scanInstance which starts with kNormal_Width, the `OS/2` value (if present), then `wdth` (if the `wdth` axis definition exists and looks sane, and uses SkFontDescriptor::SkFontStyleWidthForWidthAxisValue to convert).",
